# The crew van and the traffic (game/vehicles.ts, game/traffic.ts; docs/mechanics/driving.md). The van
# stands in Duboce's eastbound lane with someone in it. A car comes up the lane: it yields to the van as
# to a skater (its lane and stopping room grown by the van's size), stops behind it and honks. The van
# backs into it: a bump (vanBump, what car), the van stops against its bumper, the car stays on its
# lane. Then a robotaxi the same way: it stops dead (robotaxiStop), hazards on, a polite honk, and
# backing into it is a bump too. No damage, no bail: bumping is all.
park sf
cmd 0 traffic clear
cmd 1 van summon 78 -4 90
cmd 2 teleport 78 -1.6 -1.7 90
tap use 30
cmd 40 car 52 -5.4 90 9
hold down 700..900
cmd 1100 traffic clear
cmd 1101 vehicle exit
cmd 1102 van summon 78 -4 90
cmd 1103 teleport 78 -1.6 -1.7 90
tap use 1130
cmd 1140 car 52 -5.4 90 9 robo
hold down 1800..2200
run 2600
expect event vehicleEnter{name=crew_van} count == 2
expect car.car.yielding == 1 at 400
expect car.car.speed < 0.1 at 450
expect car.gap > 9 at 450
expect event honk{robo=false} within 490..505
expect event vanBump{what=car} within 990..1000
expect van.hspeed < 0.5 at 1000
expect car.pos.x < 68.5 at 1000
expect event robotaxiStop within 1260..1270
expect car.car.hazard == 1 at 1450
expect event honk{robo=true} within 1480..1490
expect event vanBump{what=robotaxi} within 2205..2215
expect event vanBump count == 2
expect no event bail
expect no event carHit
